{
  "raw": {
    "https://marybaldwin.edu/employment-and-jobs-at-mary-baldwin/": {
      "title": "Jobs and Employment",
      "description": "Employment and Jobs at Mary Baldwin — Mary Baldwin University Info Visit Give Apply Meet MBU Admissions & Aid Academics Student Experience Toggle menu More Search Results will update as you type. Close Meet MBU MBU History MBU Traditions Timeline Board of Trustees Offices Key Facts Admissions & Aid Cost and Aid Online Students Transfer Students International Students Graduate Admissions Program for the Exceptionally Gifted Early College Academics Programs and Degrees Signature – Undergrad Living & Learning Accelerated Pathways Academic Resource Center Academic Advising Study Abroad Student Experience Residential Life Online Learning Experience Life at Murphy Deming Health & Wellness Diversity & Belonging Safe and Secure Campus Virginia Women’s Institute for Leadership (VWIL) Athletics Info Visit Give Apply Quick Links Office Directory Campus Store Employment University Maps Space Reservations Information For Current Students Alumni Parents & Families Faculty & Staff Businesses & Orgs Local Communities Media Jobs and Employment at Mary Baldwin Mary Baldwin is a vibrant liberal arts school in the heart of the Shenandoah Valley, Virginia. Come join us on our mission to empower students to create lives of purpose and professional success in our changing world. Quick Links: About Mary Baldwin Open Positions Faculty Support Looking for Student Positions? Visit the McCree Center for Career Success to learn more about open student positions. Visit the McCree Center About Mary Baldwin Founded in 1842, Mary Baldwin University has a proud legacy of innovating to best serve our students as the world changes. MBU is a small, coeducational university offering a range of degree programs from bachelor to doctoral. We serve a diverse student population on our historic main campus in the heart of downtown Staunton, Virginia, Murphy Deming College of Health Sciences in nearby Fishersville, and online. MBU offers unique opportunities for our students to become leaders in the classroom, community, workplace, and in their own lives. In 1977 Mary Baldwin was the first college in Virginia to create a program for women and men to earn their degrees later in life. With the opening of our college of health sciences in 2014, we established one of the first dozen doctoral programs of occupational therapy in the nation. In 2017 we expanded on our long tradition of student-centered excellence to welcome our first residential men to campus. MBU also offers special residential programs open only to women, including the Program for the Exceptionally Gifted and the Virginia Women’s Institute for Leadership . We’re seeking forward-thinking individuals to join us at Mary Baldwin University in the beautiful Shenandoah Valley of Virginia. Together, our students, faculty, staff, and alumni create a community dedicated to bringing out the best in small, private education. Open Positions Faculty Assistant/Associate Professor – Master of Physician Assistant Studies Program Full-Time Faculty: Family Nurse Practitioner Program – Clinical Education Coordinator (Assistant/Associate Professor) Occupational Therapy Primary Faculty Staff Commandant of Cadets Housekeeper Groundskeeper/Campus Support Mailroom Coordinator Supporting our Faculty At Mary Baldwin, we know that for students to succeed, we have to support our faculty to be the best they can be. Center for Teaching and Learning The Center for Teaching and Learning serves as a resource hub where faculty can find professional development, support, and tools to enhance student outcomes and retention. McCree Center for Career Success By collaborating with the McCree Center, faculty can grow their professional network and create hands-on, real-world experiences in the classroom to improve students’ career readiness. Center for Teaching and Learning McCree Center Partnerships Equal Opportunity Employer Mary Baldwin University does not discriminate on the basis of sex or gender (*see exceptions for admission to programs within the College for Women), nor does the university discriminate on the basis of race, national or ethnic origin, color, age, disability, religion, veteran’s status, sexual orientation, gender identity, or gender expression in its educational programs, admissions, co-curricular or other activities, or employment practices. Inquiries may be directed to the Director of Human Resources, 540-887-7367, Student Activities Center 312, Mary Baldwin University, Staunton, Virginia 24401. *Exceptions within the College for Women: Virginia Women’s Institute for Leadership, Program for the Exceptionally Gifted. (November 2017) Mary Baldwin University Founded in 1842. Redesigned for today. Meet MBU Announcements Athletics Employment University Maps Campus Store MyMBU Media Contacts Alumni Community Giving News & Events Accreditation Policies Title IX Emergency Planning Campus Safety © 2023 Mary Baldwin University 101 E Frederick Street, Staunton, VA 24401 540-887-7019 info@marybaldwin.edu Social Media Directory Facebook Instagram Twitter LinkedIn TikTok YouTube"
    },
    "https://marybaldwin.edu/employment-and-jobs-at-mary-baldwin/assistant-associate-professor-master-of-physician-assistant-studies-program/": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Professor — Master of Physician Assistant Studies Program",
      "description": "Assistant/Associate Professor — Master of Physician Assistant Studies Program — Mary Baldwin University Info Visit Give Apply Meet MBU Admissions & Aid Academics Student Experience Toggle menu More Search Results will update as you type. Close Meet MBU MBU History MBU Traditions Timeline Board of Trustees Offices Key Facts Admissions & Aid Cost and Aid Online Students Transfer Students International Students Graduate Admissions Program for the Exceptionally Gifted Early College Academics Programs and Degrees Signature – Undergrad Living & Learning Accelerated Pathways Academic Resource Center Academic Advising Study Abroad Student Experience Residential Life Online Learning Experience Life at Murphy Deming Health & Wellness Diversity & Belonging Safe and Secure Campus Virginia Women’s Institute for Leadership (VWIL) Athletics Info Visit Give Apply Quick Links Office Directory Campus Store Employment University Maps Space Reservations Information For Current Students Alumni Parents & Families Faculty & Staff Businesses & Orgs Local Communities Media Employment and Jobs at Mary Baldwin Assistant/Associate Professor — Master of Physician Assistant Studies Program Murphy Deming College of Health Sciences at Mary Baldwin University invites applications for a 12-month full-time, renewable (Clinical or Scholar Pathway) Physician Assistant Faculty position beginning in September 2026. Position Summary: The Physician Assistant (MSPA) Program is fully accredited, and the dynamic faculty teaches within a unique interprofessional curriculum. We invite individuals with exceptional skills and experience in contemporary medical practice, teaching, and administration to apply. Primary responsibilities include guiding students through the PA program through teaching, advising, and mentorship. Teaching load will be determined according to expertise and program/ college needs. Candidates should be dynamic and dedicated educators who will facilitate classroom and applied learning activities while fostering an inclusive and caring learning environment. Additional responsibilities include academic advising, university, community, and professional service, and supporting the interprofessional education curriculum. Required Qualifications Master’s degree required. Must possess an unencumbered PA, NP, DO, or MD license to practice in the Commonwealth of Virginia. A minimum of 3 years of clinical experience as a Physician Assistant Strong communication, teamwork, & interpersonal skills Prefer red Qualifications Prior teaching experience is preferred, but not required Institution Information About Mary Baldwin University Founded in 1842, Mary Baldwin University has a proud legacy of innovating to best serve our students as the world changes. MBU is a small, coeducational university offering a range of degrees from bachelor to doctoral. We serve a diverse student population on our historic Staunton campus in the heart of downtown Staunton, Virginia, Murphy Deming College of Health Sciences in nearby Fishersville, and online. MBU offers unique opportunities for our students to become leaders in the classroom, community, workplace, and in their own lives. About Murphy Deming College of Health Sciences Murphy Deming College of Health Sciences (MDCHS) was opened in 2014 to address healthcare workforce needs and the complex health issues of the region. The college accomplishes this through clinically focused professional programs in Nursing, Occupational Therapy, Physical Therapy, and Physician Assistant programs that concentrate on addressing regional health care needs. We believe that community health issues are best solved by professionals who value interprofessional collaboration and thrive in a culture that embraces inclusivity and equitable access to health care. Our vision is to be recognized as the primary regional partner to develop community-oriented interventions for the education of and provision of services to the public, thereby improving health and life outcomes. To Apply: Mary Baldwin University values and celebrates diversity, is committed to equal opportunity, and does not discriminate on the basis of race, national or ethnic origin, gender identity, sexual orientation, age, disability, religion, or veteran’s status. All correspondence relating to the position of PA Faculty should be directed, in confidence, to: Tara Miller, Director of Administration & Operations for Murphy Deming twmiller@marybaldwin.edu Murphy Deming College of Health Sciences 100 Baldwin Blvd., Fishersville VA 22939 A completed application should include the following: Cover Letter outlining your interest and qualifications for the position including a statement that reflects your commitment towards supporting a culture of Equity and Inclusion Excellence. Updated CV; Three (3) professional references with contact information, title, institutional affiliation, email address and direct phone numbers. (No references will be contacted without written permission from the candidate.) The search will remain open until the position is filled.  The projected start date is fall semester, 2026. Salary range is $90,000 – $105,000 #LI-DNI #LI-DNI Announcements Athletics Employment University Maps Campus Store MyMBU Media Contacts Alumni Community Giving News & Events Accreditation Policies Title IX Emergency Planning Campus Safety © 2023 Mary Baldwin University 101 E Frederick Street, Staunton, VA 24401 540-887-7019 info@marybaldwin.edu Social Media Directory Facebook Instagram Twitter LinkedIn TikTok YouTube"
    },
    "https://marybaldwin.edu/employment-and-jobs-at-mary-baldwin/full-time-faculty-family-nurse-practitioner-program-clinical-education-coordinator-assistant-associate-professor/": {
      "title": "Full-Time Faculty: Family Nurse Practitioner Program – Clinical Education Coordinator (Assistant/Associate Professor)",
      "description": "Full-Time Faculty: Family Nurse Practitioner Program – Clinical Education Coordinator (Assistant/Associate Professor) — Mary Baldwin University Info Visit Give Apply Meet MBU Admissions & Aid Academics Student Experience Toggle menu More Search Results will update as you type. Close Meet MBU MBU History MBU Traditions Timeline Board of Trustees Offices Key Facts Admissions & Aid Cost and Aid Online Students Transfer Students International Students Graduate Admissions Program for the Exceptionally Gifted Early College Academics Programs and Degrees Signature – Undergrad Living & Learning Accelerated Pathways Academic Resource Center Academic Advising Study Abroad Student Experience Residential Life Online Learning Experience Life at Murphy Deming Health & Wellness Diversity & Belonging Safe and Secure Campus Virginia Women’s Institute for Leadership (VWIL) Athletics Info Visit Give Apply Quick Links Office Directory Campus Store Employment University Maps Space Reservations Information For Current Students Alumni Parents & Families Faculty & Staff Businesses & Orgs Local Communities Media Employment and Jobs at Mary Baldwin Full-Time Faculty: Family Nurse Practitioner Program – Clinical Education Coordinator (Assistant/Associate Professor) Position Summary: This is a 12-month, full-time Clinical Faculty position in the Family Nurse Practitioner Program for the School of Nursing in the Murphy Deming College of Health Sciences for the start of the 2026-2027 academic year. This faculty member will be responsible for teaching didactic and clinical courses within the FNP curriculum; participating in curriculum development, review, and evaluation; and mentoring and advising graduate nursing students. This faculty member will contribute to the ongoing assessment processes necessary to maintain compliance with CCNE accreditation standards. Required Qualifications Candidates must have earned a Doctor of Nursing Practice (DNP), Doctor of Philosophy (PhD) in Nursing, or a related doctoral degree from an accredited institution. Candidates with a Master of Science in Nursing (MSN) will be considered based on exceptional clinical experience, demonstrated expertise in advanced practice nursing, and a strong commitment to nursing education. Must be a nationally certified and state-licensed Family Nurse Practitioner (FNP-BC or FNP-C), with current or eligible licensure in the Commonwealth of Virginia. Minimum of three years of clinical practice experience as a Family Nurse Practitioner in a primary care or related setting. Strong interpersonal and communication skills, with the ability to effectively mentor and advise a diverse student population. Prior didactic teaching experience in a graduate nursing program is preferred; experience teaching in a Family Nurse Practitioner or other advanced practice nursing program is highly desirable. Familiarity with online and hybrid instructional delivery methods, including the use of learning management systems (e.g., Canvas), video conferencing, and other educational technologies. Experience with or understanding of simulation-based learning and curriculum development for experiential learning environments. Demonstrated commitment to learner-centered education, evidence-based teaching practices, and innovative approaches to nursing education. Prefer red Qualifications Prior experience teaching at the graduate level is preferred. Experience with online and hybrid education delivery, including the use of learning management systems and virtual instructional tools, is highly desirable. Familiarity with instructional design, student assessment, and use of technology in nursing education is highly desirable. Formal education or training in teaching, instructional technology, curriculum development, or clinical precepting (such as through a nurse educator certificate or completion of faculty development workshops) is a plus. Institution Information About Mary Baldwin University Founded in 1842, Mary Baldwin University has a proud legacy of innovating to best serve our students as the world changes. MBU is a small, coeducational university offering a range of degrees from bachelor to doctoral. We serve a diverse student population on our historic Staunton campus in the heart of downtown Staunton, Virginia, Murphy Deming College of Health Sciences in nearby Fishersville, and online. MBU offers unique opportunities for our students to become leaders in the classroom, community, workplace, and in their own lives. About Murphy Deming College of Health Sciences Murphy Deming College of Health Sciences (MDCHS) was opened in 2014 to address healthcare workforce needs and the complex health issues of the region. The college accomplishes this through clinically focused professional programs in Nursing, Occupational Therapy, Physical Therapy, and Physician Assistant programs that concentrate on addressing regional health care needs. We believe that community health issues are best solved by professionals who value interprofessional collaboration and thrive in a culture that embraces inclusivity and equitable access to health care. Our vision is to be recognized as the primary regional partner to develop community-oriented interventions for the education of and provision of services to the public, thereby improving health and life outcomes. To Apply: Mary Baldwin University is committed to promoting a culture of equity and inclusion among students, staff, and faculty. The university does not discriminate on the basis sex, gender, nor does the university discriminate on the basis of race, national or ethnic origin, color, age, disability, religion, veteran’s status, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression or any other reason prohibited by law in provision of employment opportunities and benefits. All correspondence relating to the position of FT FNP Faculty and Clinical Education Coordinator should be directed, in confidence, to: Tara Miller, Director of Administration & Operations for Murphy Deming twmiller@marybaldwin.edu Murphy Deming College of Health Sciences 100 Baldwin Blvd., Fishersville VA 22939 Cc: hr@marybaldwin.edu A completed application should include the following: Cover Letter outlining your interest and qualifications for the position including a statement that reflects your commitment towards supporting a culture of Equity and Inclusion Excellence. Updated CV; Three (3) professional references with contact information, title, institutional affiliation, email address and direct phone numbers. (No references will be contacted without written permission from the candidate.) The search will remain open until the position is filled. Annual salary is $100,000 #LI-DNI #LI-DNI Announcements Athletics Employment University Maps Campus Store MyMBU Media Contacts Alumni Community Giving News & Events Accreditation Policies Title IX Emergency Planning Campus Safety © 2023 Mary Baldwin University 101 E Frederick Street, Staunton, VA 24401 540-887-7019 info@marybaldwin.edu Social Media Directory Facebook Instagram Twitter LinkedIn TikTok YouTube"
    },
    "https://marybaldwin.edu/employment-and-jobs-at-mary-baldwin/occupational-therapy-primary-faculty/": {
      "title": "Occupational Therapy Primary Faculty",
      "description": "Occupational Therapy Primary Faculty — Mary Baldwin University Info Visit Give Apply Meet MBU Admissions & Aid Academics Student Experience Toggle menu More Search Results will update as you type. Close Meet MBU MBU History MBU Traditions Timeline Board of Trustees Offices Key Facts Admissions & Aid Cost and Aid Online Students Transfer Students International Students Graduate Admissions Program for the Exceptionally Gifted Early College Academics Programs and Degrees Signature – Undergrad Living & Learning Accelerated Pathways Academic Resource Center Academic Advising Study Abroad Student Experience Residential Life Online Learning Experience Life at Murphy Deming Health & Wellness Diversity & Belonging Safe and Secure Campus Virginia Women’s Institute for Leadership (VWIL) Athletics Info Visit Give Apply Quick Links Office Directory Campus Store Employment University Maps Space Reservations Information For Current Students Alumni Parents & Families Faculty & Staff Businesses & Orgs Local Communities Media Employment and Jobs at Mary Baldwin Occupational Therapy Primary Faculty Position Summary: Murphy Deming College of Health Sciences welcomes applications for the Occupational Therapy Primary Faculty position with an anticipated start of January 2027. This position is responsible for teaching and managing a discipline-appropriate course load using contemporary, inclusive instructional strategies and technology to support student learning and engagement. Faculty develop and maintain course materials, assess student performance fairly and consistently, mentor and advise students, and support doctoral capstone experiences. The role includes active participation in program operations, accreditation activities, recruitment, curriculum development, committee service, and collaboration with community and professional partners to support continuous program improvement. Faculty are expected to maintain professional standards through ongoing scholarship, professional development, and involvement in professional organizations while serving as positive role model for students and colleagues. Additional responsibilities include supporting college and program initiatives, maintaining accurate records and confidentiality, participating in institutional events, and performing other duties as assigned by the Program Director. Required Qualifications Doctoral degree required in occupational therapy or related field of study National Board for Certification in Occupational Therapy State licensure Three years’ experience as an occupational therapist in an occupational therapy practice setting Prefer red Qualifications Teaching experience Student interaction as clinical instructor or coordinator Institution Information About Mary Baldwin University Founded in 1842, Mary Baldwin University has a proud legacy of innovating to best serve our students as the world changes. MBU is a small, coeducational university offering a range of degrees from bachelor to doctoral. We serve a diverse student population on our historic Staunton campus in the heart of downtown Staunton, Virginia, Murphy Deming College of Health Sciences in nearby Fishersville, and online. MBU offers unique opportunities for our students to become leaders in the classroom, community, workplace, and in their own lives. About Murphy Deming College of Health Sciences Murphy Deming College of Health Sciences (MDCHS) was opened in 2014 to address healthcare workforce needs and the complex health issues of the region. The college accomplishes this through clinically focused professional programs in Nursing, Occupational Therapy, Physical Therapy, and Physician Assistant programs that concentrate on addressing regional health care needs. We believe that community health issues are best solved by professionals who value interprofessional collaboration and thrive in a culture that embraces inclusivity and equitable access to health care. Our vision is to be recognized as the primary regional partner to develop community-oriented interventions for the education of and provision of services to the public, thereby improving health and life outcomes. To Apply: Mary Baldwin University is committed to promoting a culture of equity and inclusion among students, staff, and faculty. The university does not discriminate on the basis sex, gender, nor does the university discriminate on the basis of race, national or ethnic origin, color, age, disability, religion, veteran’s status, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression or any other reason prohibited by law in provision of employment opportunities and benefits. All correspondence relating to the position of Occupational Therapy Primary Faculty should be directed, in confidence, to: Tara Miller, Director of Administration & Operations for Murphy Deming twmiller@marybaldwin.edu Murphy Deming College of Health Sciences 100 Baldwin Blvd., Fishersville VA 22939 A completed application should include the following: Cover Letter outlining your interest and qualifications for the position including a statement that reflects your commitment towards supporting a culture of Equity and Inclusion Excellence. Updated CV; Three (3) professional references with contact information, title, institutional affiliation, email address and direct phone numbers. (No references will be contacted without written permission from the candidate.) The search will remain open until the position is filled. Salary range is $80,000 – $90,000 #LI-DNI #LI-DNI #LI-DNI Announcements Athletics Employment University Maps Campus Store MyMBU Media Contacts Alumni Community Giving News & Events Accreditation Policies Title IX Emergency Planning Campus Safety © 2023 Mary Baldwin University 101 E Frederick Street, Staunton, VA 24401 540-887-7019 info@marybaldwin.edu Social Media Directory Facebook Instagram Twitter LinkedIn TikTok YouTube"
    },
    "https://marybaldwin.edu/employment-and-jobs-at-mary-baldwin/commandant-of-cadets/": {
      "title": "Commandant of Cadets",
      "description": "Commandant of Cadets — Mary Baldwin University Info Visit Give Apply Meet MBU Admissions & Aid Academics Student Experience Toggle menu More Search Results will update as you type. Close Meet MBU MBU History MBU Traditions Timeline Board of Trustees Offices Key Facts Admissions & Aid Cost and Aid Online Students Transfer Students International Students Graduate Admissions Program for the Exceptionally Gifted Early College Academics Programs and Degrees Signature – Undergrad Living & Learning Accelerated Pathways Academic Resource Center Academic Advising Study Abroad Student Experience Residential Life Online Learning Experience Life at Murphy Deming Health & Wellness Diversity & Belonging Safe and Secure Campus Virginia Women’s Institute for Leadership (VWIL) Athletics Info Visit Give Apply Quick Links Office Directory Campus Store Employment University Maps Space Reservations Information For Current Students Alumni Parents & Families Faculty & Staff Businesses & Orgs Local Communities Media Employment and Jobs at Mary Baldwin Commandant of Cadets Mary Baldwin University is currently seeking candidates for the position of Commandant of Cadets, Virginia Women’s Institute for Leadership. This is a full-time, benefits-eligible position. Position Summary: The Commandant is responsible for the overall direction and guidance of the VWIL program, Corps of Cadets, ROTC cadets, and Marching Band.  The Commandant maintains an environment in which students can balance full participation in the Corps with meaningful engagement within the university, through athletics, student government, civic engagement, and other activities. Within a 40-hour week, weekend/evening hours are expected to support cadet activities. The Commandant supervises the VWIL staff, work study cadets, and band director. Commandant’s Primary Responsibilities Coordinating with Admissions for on-campus visit days, orientations, high school visits Interfacing with Association of Military Colleges and Schools, Staunton Military Academy Alumni Foundation, the Virginia Military Institute (VMI) and service ROTC commanders Overseeing the budget process including legislative relations, writing budget language, annual report to General Assembly, meeting with representatives and military liaisons Connecting with VWIL Alumni Chapter with progress of the VWIL program and events, integrate alumni into recruitment efforts, maintain alumni database through MBU Alumni Office Representing VWIL at university meetings and functions Required Qualifications & Experience Must have a master’s degree Served successfully in the military grade of O-5 or higher, or E-7 or higher Present a high-level military appearance Maintain a level of physical conditioning to participate with cadets during physical training Supervisor experience Administrative/managerial/logistic experience Experience in leadership development for young adults in military & civilian settings High standards of performance, impeccable judgment, and character beyond reproach Demonstrated commitment to excellence Excellent communication and presentation skills, strong management, organizational skills Preferences Recent military experience (last 5 years) Instructor experience Training in a higher education environment Thorough knowledge of protocol in both military and civilian settings Must be willing to work evenings and weekends as required To Apply: Interested candidates should submit a letter of interest, resume, and contact information for three references to Commandant Search Committee at vwil@marybaldwin.edu, or via U.S. mail to P.O. Box 1500, Staunton, VA 24402.  Applications will be reviewed continuously until the position is filled. Salary Range : $80,000 – $100,000 #LI-DNI Announcements Athletics Employment University Maps Campus Store MyMBU Media Contacts Alumni Community Giving News & Events Accreditation Policies Title IX Emergency Planning Campus Safety © 2023 Mary Baldwin University 101 E Frederick Street, Staunton, VA 24401 540-887-7019 info@marybaldwin.edu Social Media Directory Facebook Instagram Twitter LinkedIn TikTok YouTube"
    },
    "https://marybaldwin.edu/employment-and-jobs-at-mary-baldwin/housekeeper-2/": {
      "title": "Housekeeper",
      "description": "Housekeeper — Mary Baldwin University Info Visit Give Apply Meet MBU Admissions & Aid Academics Student Experience Toggle menu More Search Results will update as you type. Close Meet MBU MBU History MBU Traditions Timeline Board of Trustees Offices Key Facts Admissions & Aid Cost and Aid Online Students Transfer Students International Students Graduate Admissions Program for the Exceptionally Gifted Early College Academics Programs and Degrees Signature – Undergrad Living & Learning Accelerated Pathways Academic Resource Center Academic Advising Study Abroad Student Experience Residential Life Online Learning Experience Life at Murphy Deming Health & Wellness Diversity & Belonging Safe and Secure Campus Virginia Women’s Institute for Leadership (VWIL) Athletics Info Visit Give Apply Quick Links Office Directory Campus Store Employment University Maps Space Reservations Information For Current Students Alumni Parents & Families Faculty & Staff Businesses & Orgs Local Communities Media Employment and Jobs at Mary Baldwin Housekeeper Position Summary: Mary Baldwin University currently has positions available for Housekeepers.  Reporting to the Custodial Services Supervisor, this position provides general cleaning services and is a full-time, 40 hours per week position with benefits.  Rate of pay is $15 an hour. Key responsibilities include, but are not limited to: Sweeping, dust/wet mopping, and vacuuming of floors Cleaning of offices and residence halls, including common areas Cleaning of restrooms, including fixtures, dispensers, toilets, showers/tubs Trash collection in offices/residence halls Other duties as assigned Minimum qualifications Knowledge of basic cleaning procedures and ability to follow written and oral instructions Previous experience cleaning in a university or institutional setting preferred, but not required Must be able to lift/carry items weighing up to 20 lbs. Valid driver’s license To Apply: Interested candidates may apply by sending a resume to Misty Miller, Housekeeping Supervisor, at mmiller@marybaldwin.edu , or complete an application at the MBU Facilities Office at 318 Prospect St., Staunton, VA 24401 #LI-DNI #LI-DNI Announcements Athletics Employment University Maps Campus Store MyMBU Media Contacts Alumni Community Giving News & Events Accreditation Policies Title IX Emergency Planning Campus Safety © 2023 Mary Baldwin University 101 E Frederick Street, Staunton, VA 24401 540-887-7019 info@marybaldwin.edu Social Media Directory Facebook Instagram Twitter LinkedIn TikTok YouTube"
    },
    "https://marybaldwin.edu/employment-and-jobs-at-mary-baldwin/groundskeeper-campus-support/": {
      "title": "Groundskeeper/Campus Support",
      "description": "Groundskeeper/Campus Support — Mary Baldwin University Info Visit Give Apply Meet MBU Admissions & Aid Academics Student Experience Toggle menu More Search Results will update as you type. Close Meet MBU MBU History MBU Traditions Timeline Board of Trustees Offices Key Facts Admissions & Aid Cost and Aid Online Students Transfer Students International Students Graduate Admissions Program for the Exceptionally Gifted Early College Academics Programs and Degrees Signature – Undergrad Living & Learning Accelerated Pathways Academic Resource Center Academic Advising Study Abroad Student Experience Residential Life Online Learning Experience Life at Murphy Deming Health & Wellness Diversity & Belonging Safe and Secure Campus Virginia Women’s Institute for Leadership (VWIL) Athletics Info Visit Give Apply Quick Links Office Directory Campus Store Employment University Maps Space Reservations Information For Current Students Alumni Parents & Families Faculty & Staff Businesses & Orgs Local Communities Media Employment and Jobs at Mary Baldwin Groundskeeper/Campus Support Position Summary: Mary Baldwin University is seeking proactive and energetic individuals for the position of Groundskeeper/Campus Support. Reporting to the Maintenance & Grounds Supervisor, this is a 40 hours per week, full-time position with benefits.  Pay rate is $15 per hour. Overview of Position Groundskeeper duties include mowing, weeding, trimming, planting, trash removal, mulching, and snow removal.  Campus Support duties include set-up for campus events, delivery of supplies and equipment, and moving furniture. Groundskeepers work primarily outside, in all seasons and weather.  As essential personnel, work may be required occasionally on weekends and when the University is closed due to inclement weather. Minimum qualifications High school diploma or equivalent preferred. Valid Driver’s License and good driving record required. Heavy physical labor is involved, so must be able to lift and carry at least 50 lbs. Ability to communicate clearly and effectively. Must pass a background check. To Apply: Interested applicants may submit a resume to bkwhetzel@marybaldwin.edu or complete an application, which can be obtained at the Facilities Management Office at 318 Prospect St. Staunton, VA 24401. For more information, call 540-887-7209. #LI-DNI #LI-DNI #LI-DNI Announcements Athletics Employment University Maps Campus Store MyMBU Media Contacts Alumni Community Giving News & Events Accreditation Policies Title IX Emergency Planning Campus Safety © 2023 Mary Baldwin University 101 E Frederick Street, Staunton, VA 24401 540-887-7019 info@marybaldwin.edu Social Media Directory Facebook Instagram Twitter LinkedIn TikTok YouTube"
    },
    "https://marybaldwin.edu/employment-and-jobs-at-mary-baldwin/mailroom-coordinator/": {
      "title": "Mailroom Coordinator",
      "description": "Mailroom Coordinator — Mary Baldwin University Info Visit Give Apply Meet MBU Admissions & Aid Academics Student Experience Toggle menu More Search Results will update as you type. Close Meet MBU MBU History MBU Traditions Timeline Board of Trustees Offices Key Facts Admissions & Aid Cost and Aid Online Students Transfer Students International Students Graduate Admissions Program for the Exceptionally Gifted Early College Academics Programs and Degrees Signature – Undergrad Living & Learning Accelerated Pathways Academic Resource Center Academic Advising Study Abroad Student Experience Residential Life Online Learning Experience Life at Murphy Deming Health & Wellness Diversity & Belonging Safe and Secure Campus Virginia Women’s Institute for Leadership (VWIL) Athletics Info Visit Give Apply Quick Links Office Directory Campus Store Employment University Maps Space Reservations Information For Current Students Alumni Parents & Families Faculty & Staff Businesses & Orgs Local Communities Media Employment and Jobs at Mary Baldwin Mailroom Coordinator Position Summary: Mary Baldwin University is currently seeking a Mailroom Coordinator.  This position reports to the Director of Campus Support Services.  This is a full-time, non-exempt, benefits-eligible position.  Hourly rate is $15.75. Manages the daily operations of the MBU mailroom by receiving, sorting, preparing, and delivering mail and packages across campus. Provides customer service to students, faculty, staff, and campus partners. Maintains accurate records for efficient mailroom operations. Primary Duties Mail Processing — Receive, sort, and prepare incoming and outgoing mail & packages. Customer Service — Provide window service, assist customers with mailing procedures, and respond to email and phone inquiries. Student Worker Coordination — Direct, support, and mentor student assistants assigned to the mail room while fostering a respectful and inclusive team environment. Recordkeeping & Organization — Maintain forms, logs, and operational documentation; ensure organized filing systems and general upkeep of the mail room. Bulk Mail Support — Coordinate bulk mailing requirements with campus departments to ensure proper preparation, postage accuracy, and timely delivery. Shipping & Packaging — Assist departments with packaging, documentation, and shipping procedures. Operational Efficiency — Analyze and report utilization efficiencies for mail service platforms, machines, and shipping services across campus. Financial Support — Assist with ordering supplies and invoicing departments as needed. Campus Engagement — Effectively market mailroom services to campus partners and the community and maintain positive relationships with customers and departments. Problem Resolution — Address workplace, employee, and customer concerns to ensure smooth operations. Share space and coordinate schedules with Print Services. Other duties as assigned. Required Qualifications High School Diploma or equivalent. Valid Virginia driver’s license. Ability to learn and apply U.S. Postal Service regulations (prior knowledge preferred but not required). Strong attention to detail, adaptability, and organizational skills. Ability to maintain cleanliness and uphold a professional, positive, and respectful attitude. Demonstrated reliability, punctuality, and ability to represent MBU responsibly. Physical Requirements Ability to lift and carry up to 50 lbs. independently; heavier items with assistance. Frequent reaching, stooping, kneeling, walking, and stair climbing while carrying loads. Ability to stand or walk for extended periods. Sufficient manual dexterity to operate mailroom equipment. Good vision and hearing (with or without corrective devices). Work performed indoors and outdoors in all weather conditions. To Apply: Interested candidates may apply by sending a cover letter and resume to Kay Shirey, Director of Campus Support Services, at ceshirey@marybaldwin.edu . #LI-DNI #LI-DNI #LI-DNI Announcements Athletics Employment University Maps Campus Store MyMBU Media Contacts Alumni Community Giving News & Events Accreditation Policies Title IX Emergency Planning Campus Safety © 2023 Mary Baldwin University 101 E Frederick Street, Staunton, VA 24401 540-887-7019 info@marybaldwin.edu Social Media Directory Facebook Instagram Twitter LinkedIn TikTok YouTube"
    }
  },
